    "Times are park time. Moonrise and moonset are good to about a quarter of an hour, planets to about a degree. In the sky, the Moon is drawn larger than life so its phase reads; its place is true.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Times are park time. Moonrise and moonset are good to about a quarter of an hour, planets to about a degree. In the sky, the Moon is drawn larger than life so its phase reads; its place is true."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Las horas son las del parque. La salida y la puesta de la Luna tienen un margen de unos quince minutos; los planetas, de un grado. En el cielo, la Luna se dibuja más grande de lo real para que se lea su fase; su posición es la verdadera."
          }
        }
      }
    },
